course: dictionary
lesson: 2379
title: Cupful, a measure of amount
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cupful is an amount, not an object. It tells you how much a cup holds, so «two cupfuls of flour» means two cups' worth of flour.
explain: In a recipe, a cupful is a measure of about one cup of an ingredient. When you do not have a measuring jug, a cupful gives you a rough idea of how much to use.
explain: Look at the words around it. In «half a cupful», the word half tells you the amount is halved. In «a cupful of water», the word of tells you what is being measured.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Add a cupful of milk» still makes sense if you read it as "add the amount a cup holds of milk."
fact: A cupful is an amount: the amount that a cup holds.
fact: In cooking, a cupful is a measure of about one cup of an ingredient, such as flour or sugar.
fact: The plural is cupfuls, but cupsful is also used.
fact: «Half a cupful» means half the amount a cup holds.
fact: A cupful tells you how much, not what the cup looks like: «a cupful of oil weighs less than a cupful of water» compares two equal amounts of different liquids.
exercise: «Add two cupfuls of flour to the bowl.» What does cupful tell you? | A kind of spoon | *How much flour, the amount a cup holds | The name of the flour | The shape of the bowl
exercise: «A cupful of oil weighs less than a cupful of water.» Which statement is true? | A cupful of oil weighs more than a cupful of water | Oil and water always weigh exactly the same | *A cupful of oil weighs less than a cupful of water | Oil is a kind of cup
exercise: Which phrase means half the amount a cup holds? | A cup-shaped hat | A whole pool of tears | *Half a cupful | Three cupfuls
test: In «even a long cry makes far less than a cupful», which is the biggest amount? | *A cupful | A single tear | Two drops | A long cry
test: In a recipe, what does a cupful mean? | *About one cup of an ingredient | A size of shoe | A small spoon | A kind of oven
exam: Ben says a cupful is a cup you drink from. What is the best correction? | Cupful is the name of a cup | Cupful means a kind of tea | Cupful means empty | *Cupful is an amount, the amount a cup holds, not the cup itself
